column44:
Main Similarities
both are relevant to live audio capture;
both operate on sample frames;
both are useful in recording/input pipelines;
both can participate in tracking capture position;
both expose information tied to the audio capture/render timeline.

Apple's documentation specifically states that AudioUnitRender receives the number of audio sample frames involved in the render operation and an associated audio timestamp.

Main Residual Differences
GetFramesRead is a query.
AudioUnitRender is a capture/render operation.
GetFramesRead directly returns a cumulative count.
AudioUnitRender provides per-render frame quantities/timestamps; cumulative accounting is application-managed.
AUHAL setup requires additional configuration and lifecycle APIs.

